#: ../../errors.rst:3
msgid "Error messages"
msgstr "エラーメッセージ"

#: ../../errors.rst:6
msgid ""
"A report should name the problem, show its location, and give a useful "
"next step. Guidedog keeps that evidence as structured data. The terminal "
"adds color and a source marker. JSON keeps the data without terminal "
"decoration."
msgstr ""
"診断は問題の名前、場所、役立つ次の操作を示すべきです。Guidedog "
"はその情報を構造化データとして保持します。端末では色とソースの印を付けます。JSON は装飾なしでデータを保持します。"

#: ../../errors.rst:10
msgid "Reading a report"
msgstr "診断の読み方"

#: ../../errors.rst:25
msgid "A report has four parts, always in this order:"
msgstr "診断は常に次の順序で、4 つの部分からなります。"

#: ../../errors.rst:27
#, fuzzy
#| msgid ""
#| "**The title bar.** The title names the kind of problem in capitals; "
#| "warnings and notes start with ``WARNING:`` and ``NOTE:``. At the right "
#| "of the bar is the report's code, such as "
#| "``rst.substitution.undefined``: a stable name you can search for."
msgid ""
"**The title bar.** The title names the kind of problem in capitals. "
"Warnings and notes start with ``WARNING:`` and ``NOTE:``. At the right of "
"the bar is the report's code, such as ``rst.substitution.undefined``: a "
"stable name we can search for."
msgstr ""
"**タイトル行。**\\ 問題の種類を大文字で示します。警告と注記は ``WARNING:`` と ``NOTE:`` で始まります。右端の "
"``rst.substitution.undefined`` などは、検索に使える安定した診断コードです。"

#: ../../errors.rst:30
msgid ""
"**Where.** The file and line, the source line itself, and a marker under "
"the text the problem is about. A problem that is not about one line (a "
"missing folder, a flag) shows only the path, or nothing."
msgstr ""
"**場所。**\\ "
"ファイル、行番号、ソースの行と問題箇所の下の印を示します。ディレクトリ不足やオプションなど、特定の行に関係しない問題ではパスだけ、または場所なしで表示します。"

#: ../../errors.rst:33
msgid ""
"**What happened.** The explanation, followed, when it matters, by what "
"the problem means for the output: here, that nothing was written."
msgstr "**何が起きたか。**\\ 問題を説明し、必要なら出力への影響も示します。この例では何も書き出していないことです。"

#: ../../errors.rst:35
msgid ""
"**What to do.** The hint, in green on a color terminal: a concrete "
"direction. Where there are several ways to fix the problem, the hint "
"names them, the most likely first."
msgstr "**何をすべきか。**\\ カラー端末では緑で示す、具体的な修正方法です。複数ある場合は、最も可能性の高い方法から列挙します。"

#: ../../errors.rst:39
#, fuzzy
#| msgid ""
#| "Colors only underline what the words already say; ``--color=never`` "
#| "turns them off and ``--color=always`` keeps them when the output is "
#| "not a terminal."
msgid ""
"Colors only underline what the words already say. ``--color=never`` turns "
"them off. ``--color=always`` keeps them when the output is not a terminal."
msgstr ""
"色は文章で伝えた内容を強調するだけです。\\ ``--color=never`` で色を無効にし、\\ ``--color=always`` "
"で端末以外の出力にも色を残せます。"

#: ../../errors.rst:42
msgid "Every hint gives directions"
msgstr "次の操作を示すヒント"

#: ../../errors.rst:45
#, fuzzy
#| msgid ""
#| "Guidedog holds its own messages to this: a hint starts with what to do "
#| "(\"Add\", \"Pass\", \"Set\", \"Rename\", \"Run\") and names what to do "
#| "it to, such as ``--budget=MIB``, ``root_doc`` in ``conf.toml``, or the "
#| "directive's option. A test (``tests/hints_test.odin``) reads every "
#| "message Guidedog can emit and fails when a hint is empty, repeats the "
#| "message, or says only \"report this\" without saying what to report "
#| "with. Two forms are allowed because they name the fix themselves: a "
#| "suggestion (\"Did you mean numfig?\") and, for a note that needs no "
#| "action, \"Nothing to do:\" with the reason."
msgid ""
"Guidedog holds its own messages to this rule. A hint starts with what to "
"do (\"Add\", \"Pass\", \"Set\", \"Rename\", \"Run\"). It names what to do "
"it to, such as ``--budget=MIB``, ``root_doc`` in ``conf.toml``, or the "
"directive's option. Tests check the messages Guidedog emits. They fail "
"when a hint is empty, repeats the message, or says only \"report this\" "
"without saying what to report with. Two other forms are allowed, because "
"they name the fix themselves. One is a suggestion (\"Did you mean "
"numfig?\"). The other, for a note that needs no action, is \"Nothing to "
"do:\" with the reason."
msgstr ""
"Guidedog "
"自身のメッセージにもこの規則を課す。ヒントは操作（「Add」「Pass」「Set」「Rename」「Run」）と、その対象を示す。例えば "
"``--budget=MIB``\\ 、\\ ``conf.toml`` の ``root_doc``\\ 、ディレクティブのオプションだ。\\ "
"``tests/hints_test.odin`` は全メッセージを読み、空のヒント、本文の繰り返し、報告内容を示さない「report "
"this」を拒否する。修正を直接示す提案（「Did you mean numfig?」）と、操作不要の注記「Nothing to "
"do:」に理由を添える形式も認める。"

#: ../../errors.rst:52
#, fuzzy
#| msgid ""
#| "When the problem is Guidedog's own fault, the hint says so and asks "
#| "you to report it with the command you ran, the input that caused it, "
#| "and the output of ``guidedog --version``."
msgid ""
"When the problem is Guidedog's own fault, the hint says so. It asks us to "
"report it with the command we ran, the input that caused it, and the "
"output of ``guidedog --version``."
msgstr ""
"Guidedog 自身の不具合なら、そのことを明示します。実行したコマンド、原因となった入力、\\ ``guidedog --version`` "
"の出力を添えて報告するよう案内します。"

#: ../../errors.rst:56
msgid "Reports for programs"
msgstr "プログラム向けの診断"

#: ../../errors.rst:59
msgid ""
"``--diagnostics=json`` writes each report as one JSON object per line on "
"standard error, for editors and continuous integration:"
msgstr ""
"``--diagnostics=json`` は標準エラーに一行一個の JSON "
"オブジェクトとして報告を書く。エディターや継続的インテグレーションから読める。"

#: ../../errors.rst:70
#, fuzzy
#| msgid ""
#| "(shown wrapped here; each object is on one line). ``schema`` is the "
#| "version of this format, which changes only when a field does; check it "
#| "before reading the rest. Columns count Unicode scalars, not bytes or "
#| "terminal cells, from 1. ``source`` is the complete original source "
#| "line; the terminal shows a bounded window around the error and aligns "
#| "its caret after escaping controls and measuring wide characters. "
#| "``category`` is the warning's category, as ``suppress_warnings`` names "
#| "it, or empty."
msgid ""
"(shown wrapped here; each object is on one line). ``schema`` is the "
"version of this format. It changes only when a field does, so a program "
"checks it before reading the rest. Columns count Unicode scalars, not "
"bytes or terminal cells, from 1. ``source`` is the complete original "
"source line. The terminal shows a bounded window around the error. It "
"aligns its caret after escaping controls and measuring wide characters. "
"``category`` is the warning's category, as ``suppress_warnings`` names "
"it, or empty."
msgstr ""
"ここでは折り返して示すが、実際は一オブジェクト一行。\\ ``schema`` "
"はフィールドが変わったときだけ更新する形式の版で、他を読む前に確認する。列は1から始まる Unicode "
"スカラー数で、バイト数や端末の桁数ではない。\\ ``source`` "
"は元の行全体。端末はエラー周辺だけを表示し、制御文字のエスケープと全角文字の幅を考慮して印を合わせる。\\ ``category`` は "
"``suppress_warnings`` で使う警告分類、または空。"

#: ../../errors.rst:77
msgid "When memory runs out"
msgstr "メモリが足りないとき"

#: ../../errors.rst:80
#, fuzzy
#| msgid ""
#| "Running out of memory is a report too, never a crash. There are two "
#| "kinds:"
msgid "Reaching a bound is a report, not a crash. There are two kinds:"
msgstr "メモリ不足も診断として報告し、クラッシュしません。2 種類あります。"

#: ../../errors.rst:82
msgid "``host.budget`` (MEMORY BUDGET REACHED)"
msgstr "``host.budget``\\ （メモリ予算の上限）"

#: ../../errors.rst:83
#, fuzzy
#| msgid ""
#| "The build reached the memory it may hold, its budget "
#| "(``--budget=MIB``, 1 GiB by default). The report names the step and, "
#| "for a template, the line that asked for the memory. At a terminal the "
#| "build asks once what to do: raise the budget to one the step fits, go "
#| "on with the working memory on disk, or stop; elsewhere it stops, and "
#| "``--budget`` or ``--memory=disk`` chooses ahead. The hint names that "
#| "same budget as a number, for example:"
msgid ""
"The build reached the memory it may hold, its budget (``--budget=MIB``, 1 "
"GiB by default). The budget counts what Guidedog reads and keeps: "
"sources, included files, and the PDF the embedded Typst compiler returns. "
"The report names the step and the file that needed the memory. The hint "
"names a budget that fits, as a number. For example:"
msgstr ""
"ビルドが保持可能なメモリ予算（\\ ``--budget=MIB``\\ 、既定 1 "
"GiB）に達した。報告は該当の工程を、テンプレートなら要求元の行も示す。端末では一度だけ、予算を増やすか、作業メモリをディスクに置いて続けるか、停止するかを尋ねる。端末以外では停止する。\\ "
"``--budget`` または ``--memory=disk`` で事前に選べる。ヒントも予算を数値で示す。"

#: ../../errors.rst:91
#, fuzzy
#| msgid ""
#| "The number holds what the build held and the refused step four times "
#| "over (the step also holds its output and the copy it writes), or twice "
#| "the old budget, whichever is larger, rounded up to 64 MiB, and no more "
#| "than the memory the machine has free when the step fits there. When it "
#| "does not, the hint says so, and names ``--memory=disk`` first:"
msgid ""
"The number is the larger of two figures. One is what the build held plus "
"four times the refused step (the step also holds its output and the copy "
"it writes). The other is twice the old budget. The number is rounded up "
"to 64 MiB. It is no more than the memory the machine has free, when the "
"step fits there. When it does not, the hint says so:"
msgstr ""
"提案値は、現在の保持量に拒否された工程の要求量を4倍して加えた量（工程は出力と書き込み用コピーも保持する）と旧予算の2倍の大きい方を、64 MiB "
"単位で切り上げる。工程が空きメモリに収まる場合はその空き量を超えない。収まらない場合はその旨を示し、まず ``--memory=disk`` "
"を提案する。"

#: ../../errors.rst:99
msgid ""
"``GUIDEDOG_AVAILABLE_MIB`` states the machine's free memory when the "
"system's own figure misleads, for example inside a container."
msgstr ""

#: ../../errors.rst:102
msgid "``host.memory`` (OUT OF MEMORY)"
msgstr "``host.memory``\\ （メモリ不足）"

#: ../../errors.rst:103
#, fuzzy
#| msgid ""
#| "The system refused memory the budget allowed. The command stops "
#| "without using what it was refused: a build publishes nothing, a GDS "
#| "change is applied whole or not at all, and ``convert`` writes a whole "
#| "page or none. Free memory, or build with fewer threads (``-j 1``), and "
#| "run the command again. Once a build has decided to publish, switching "
#| "its output into place needs no memory, so a refusal cannot stop a "
#| "publication halfway; if the build instead finds an earlier build's "
#| "publication to finish and has no memory to plan it, it leaves that "
#| "publication as it was, for the next build."
msgid ""
"The system could not provide a buffer the budget allowed. The command "
"stops without using it. A build publishes nothing, a GDS change is "
"applied whole or not at all, and ``convert`` writes a whole page or none. "
"Free memory, or build with fewer threads (``-j 1``), and run the command "
"again. Once a build has decided to publish, switching its output into "
"place needs no further planning. So a refusal cannot stop a publication "
"halfway. The next build finishes an interrupted publication."
msgstr ""
"予算内の要求をシステムが拒否した。命令はそのメモリを使わず停止する。ビルドは公開せず、GDS の変更は全部か無変更、\\ ``convert`` "
"は一ページ全部か無出力となる。メモリを解放するかスレッドを減らして（\\ ``-j 1``\\ "
"）再実行する。公開を決定した後の切り替えはメモリを必要とせず、拒否で半公開にはならない。以前の未完了の公開を見つけても復旧計画のメモリがなければ、そのまま次のビルドに残す。"

#: ../../errors.rst:110
msgid ""
"A document's own size is bounded separately, by ``--max-nodes``, "
"``--max-depth`` and ``--stack-kib``. An oversized document is reported "
"with the limit it reached. See :doc:`internals/memory` for how the budget "
"and these limits divide the work. The Odin implementation could also keep "
"working memory on disk (``--memory=disk``). The Rust implementation "
"bounds a conversion by its limits instead, so there is no disk mode."
msgstr ""

